-- title:
--   Twelve divides ordₓ T-ordₓ J at cusps
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\kappa$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, let $M\ge 5$ be a nonzero natural number with $p\nmid M$, and let $K_0=$ [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC κ M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$ generated by the ratios of $q$-expansions of integral modular forms for $\Gamma_1(M)$. Let $w$ be an integral weight-one form for $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $\kappa$, that is, a modular form $f$ of weight $1$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with a power series $p_1\in\mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ whose image in $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$ is the $q$-expansion of $f$ and whose image $\bar p_1$ in $\kappa((q))$ is nonzero. Let $J,T\in K_0$ be elements whose underlying Laurent series are, respectively, $q^{-1}$ times the reduction to $\kappa$ of $\mathrm{jNum}=E_4^3\cdot\Delta^{-1}$-numerator (so $J$ is the reduction $\bar\jmath$ of the $j$-expansion), and the quotient of the reduction of $p_1^{12}$ by the reduction of $q\prod_{n\ge 1}(1-q^n)^{24}$ (the $q$-expansion of $\Delta$). Finally let $x$ be a place of $K_0$ over $\kappa$, i.e. a valuation subring of $K_0$ containing $\kappa$, different from $K_0$ and a principal ideal ring, with associated order function $\operatorname{ord}_x$, and assume $\operatorname{ord}_x J<0$. Then $12$ divides $\operatorname{ord}_x T-\operatorname{ord}_x J$ in $\mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   The places with $\operatorname{ord}_x J<0$ are the cusps of $X_1(M)_\kappa$, of width $-\operatorname{ord}_x J$; the statement is the cusp counterpart of the corresponding $12$-divisibility of $\operatorname{ord}_x T$ at the places where $J$ is regular, and together the two say that $\operatorname{ord}_x T-\min(0,\operatorname{ord}_x J)$ lies in $12\mathbb{Z}$ at every place, so that the order of vanishing of the weight-one form read through $T=f^{12}/\Delta$ is an integer. It is used in the computation of ramification indices for the Igusa function field of $X_1(M)_\kappa$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_twelve_dvd_ord_sub_ord_of_coe_eq_div_of_ord_neg_x1FunctionFieldC.lean

